Make the Controls help page a pad reference card.

Upstream's Controls page lists key names, which is the right page for a desktop and the
wrong one for a console: there is no keyboard in the room, and the one thing a player
genuinely cannot work out for themselves is which of the four face buttons changes the
camera.

So it becomes a reference card - the shared controller wireframe from
`common/assets/controls`, with the bindings beside it. Read-only on purpose: rebinding is
a much bigger screen than this port needs, and the actions on the left do not change when
a future upstream renumbers a button.

**The page already existed**, which is why this is a patch to one function rather than a
new state and a new menu entry. `PAGE_CONTROLS` is in upstream's help screen, reachable
from the title screen at any time, and it already had the tab.

The buttons named here are the ones patch 0009 sets, which are this pad's rather than the
DualShock 3 order upstream assumes - so "Hold L3" for fast rotation is not a typo, it is
where a trigger-less index had to go.

The artwork ships in the *packaged* data as `gui/oops-controller.png` - copied there by
this title's `package` rule - so upstream's own `data/` stays exactly as upstream ships
it.

The page also says motion tilt exists, where to turn it on, and how to re-centre it,
because a feature that is off by default and mentioned nowhere is a feature that is not
there - and because the first thing a player tries when the floor sits tipped is putting
the pad flat on a table, which cannot work: the level reference is the port's, not the
sensor's, so only a deliberate click can clear it.

